\date{2024-07-26}
\taxon{Theorem}
\author{fredrikbakke}
\meta{source}{Theorem 3.1.6 of [[MR23]]}
\import{common}

\p{Suppose the crisp type family #{{G \colon-flat I \to \Type}} [detects continuity](fb-0046) for #{{\flat \dashv \sharp}} and assume given a crisp map #{{f \colon-flat X \to Y}}. Then #{f} is an [[hott-000U]] if (and only if) #{{\modflat{f} \colon \modflat{X} \to \modflat{Y}}} is an equivalence and for all #{{i :^\flat I}}, the map
##{\modflat{f \o \blank} \colon \modflat{G_i \to X} \to \modflat{G_i \to Y}}
is an equivalence.}
